# UniVerse: working rules

Start with `START-HERE.md` (where things stand, how to run it). The plan is
`apps/web/STAGE-5-PLAN.md` (section 4 "Remaining work queue", and the **Progress** table at the
end); notes per item are in `apps/web/STAGE-5-HANDOFF.md`. The app is all in `apps/web`. Also read
`apps/web/AGENTS.md`: this is **Next.js 16**, which differs from older versions; check
`node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using a Next.js API.

## Working with the owner

- The owner is not a developer: explain in plain words, short and concrete (what they can now do,
  what they need to do). No jargon without a one-line meaning.
- Work through the plan's queue in order (next: **Q14**). **One commit per item**; push at
  checkpoints. Each finished item gets a **Progress row** in `STAGE-5-PLAN.md` (what was built,
  where, how it was tested, what's not done) and a short note in `STAGE-5-HANDOFF.md` (traps, rules
  for code that builds on it, the next migration number). Mark the item's heading ✅.
- **Merge only when the owner says "merge"**, each time. Don't open a pull request unless asked.
- Anything that **costs money or needs an account** (a paid service, Workers Paid, SMS, app stores,
  Google/Microsoft apps, Razorpay): ask first; build it behind a switch, off, and mark it **[owner]**.

## Safety (never break these)

- **Never handle real secrets.** Real keys live only in the Cloudflare dashboard. Local tests use
  placeholder values on the command line (`pnpm local:serve --ai-placeholder`); never write keys in
  `.dev.vars`, `.env*` or any committed file, and never paste them in chat.
- **No AI model names or IDs** in commit messages, pull requests or code comments.
- **Never weaken sign-in or access checks** (`src/server/auth.ts`, `src/lib/server-auth.ts`,
  `src/server/access.ts`). The local **demo admin is read-only by design**: don't get around it;
  test admin saving with unit tests (mocked Prisma) instead.
- **Request data is untrusted**: read bodies and queries through `src/server/body.ts` (`oneOf`,
  `str`, `text`, `strings`, `first`) and give Prisma only `pick<Prisma.XInput>(body, keys)`
  (`src/server/pick.ts`). Every route that serves people's data checks who is asking.

## Product rules

- **No new emails.** Notify in the app: `notify` / `notifyMany` from `src/server/email.ts` with
  `email: false`.
- New features go **inside existing menus, as tabs**, not new top-level pages.
- Motion: `import { m as motion } from 'framer-motion'` and the springs in `src/lib/motion.ts`.
  Links: only `@/components/ui/Link`.
- **No polling.** Live updates: `publish()` (`src/server/realtime.ts`) plus a `useLiveInterval`
  fallback, or `useActivePoll` for screens without live updates (`src/lib/realtime-client.ts`).
- **AI** always: `spendAi` (daily allowance), `featureOff('ai')` (the owner's switch), and the AI
  cache (`cachedAi` / `saveAi`) when everyone would get the same answer. Show AI answers with
  `MathText` and put `MATH_RULE` in prompts (`src/lib/tutor-rules.ts`).
- **Sample mode** (the public demo without a database): every new GET route gets a stub in
  `src/lib/sample/router.ts`; writes call `notice()`.
- Accessibility: every screen axe-clean (serious/critical) at **390 and 1280 px, light and dark**,
  and no sideways scrolling.

## Platform limits (Cloudflare Workers Free)

- **D1: at most 100 bound values per query** (chunk lists by 90; multi-row inserts with N rows a
  statement) and **at most 50 queries per request**. D1 has no transactions.
- The build machine has 8 GB, 2 CPUs and 20 minutes: keep heavy libraries out of first-load bundles
  (dynamic `import()`).
- The light API path (`cloudflare/fast-api.ts`) must run the same code as its Next route; the startup
  bundle keys (`src/lib/bootstrap.ts`) must match the head script.

## Database changes

Hand-written SQL in `apps/web/prisma/migrations/NNNN_name.sql` (**next: 0157**) plus
`prisma/schema.prisma`; then, from `apps/web`:
`PRISMA_GENERATE_SKIP_AUTOINSTALL=1 npx prisma generate`,
`npx wrangler d1 migrations apply universe-db --local`, `node scripts/gen-owner-schema.mjs`.
A new API route: `node scripts/gen-api-routes.mjs`. Deploys apply new migrations themselves.

## Before every commit

- `pnpm check` (from `apps/web`): `pnpm typecheck` (the only type check: the deploy build skips it),
  eslint on changed files (**0 errors**, the whole repo under 50 warnings, **no disable comments**:
  fix the cause), and the unit tests (`npx vitest run`).
- For screens: `pnpm local:build`, `pnpm local:serve`, then a Playwright + axe check like those in
  `apps/web/scripts/checks/` (no screenshots needed). Don't edit source files while a build runs.
  Never commit changes the build makes to `public/sw.js`, `public/fallback-*.js`,
  `public/workbox-*.js` or `apps/web/cloudflare/next-public.gen.ts` (`local:build` puts them back).

## Optional: Everything Claude Code (ECC)

The owner may want **Everything Claude Code** (github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code), a large
add-on pack for Claude Code (and partly Cursor): agents, skills, slash commands, rules, hooks.
Rules for using it here:
- **Don't install the whole pack**: its catalogue is sent with every request (slower, costlier).
  Install a minimal profile or pick single pieces (e.g. a planning or review skill).
- **Read every hook before turning it on**: hooks run commands automatically. Never enable anything
  that sends code or data to another service (some commands send diffs to other AI providers).
- It never overrides this file: the owner's rules, safety rules and the plan come first.
- Ask the owner before installing it, and say what you're adding and why.

## Gotchas already learned

- React hooks lint (v6): no reading refs while rendering, no `setState` directly in an effect body
  (in a callback or a promise is fine), no reassigning variables after render, no `Date.now()` while
  rendering (`src/lib/use-now.ts`).
- axe "label-content-name-mismatch": don't give a button an `aria-label` different from its visible
  text; add `sr-only` text instead. An absolutely positioned `sr-only` span inside an
  `overflow-x-auto` toolbar can widen the page: make the toolbar `relative`.
- ProseMirror reads a keyboard selection a moment after the key: pause ~150 ms in browser tests
  before a toolbar action.
- Attendance rows are stored at midnight UTC of the class day. D1 supports FTS5 and window functions.
- KaTeX: import `katex/dist/katex.mjs` (plain `katex` may be the CommonJS copy that the chemistry
  extension doesn't extend).
- In browser tests, measure elements only after the calendar's days finish sliding in; phone tab
  bars can cover elements near the bottom (scroll them into the middle first).
